{title: He Calls His Own by Name}
{subtitle: John 10:1–18}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [C] | ×2
| [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]At the gate of the sheepfold in the early light of day
The gatekeeper opens and the shepherd leads the way
He [Bb]calls his own [C]sheep by name and [Gm]leads them out
And they [Bb]follow where he goes, [C]for they know his [Dm]voice
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I am the good shepherd
The [C]good shepherd lays down his life for the [Dm]sheep
I know [Bb]my own [F]and my [C]own know [Dm]me
And I [Bb]lay down my [C]life for the [Dm]sheep
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The thief comes only to [Bb]steal and [C]kill and de[Dm]stroy
But the shepherd brings his flock to pas[Bb]ture and [C]to [Dm]joy
When [Bb]the wolf comes [F]down the hired [C]hand will [Gm]run
But [Bb]the shepherd stands his ground [C]for every single [Dm]one
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I am the good shepherd
The [C]good shepherd lays down his life for the [Dm]sheep
I know [Bb]my own and [F]my own [C]know [Dm]me
And I [Bb]lay down my [C]life for the [Dm]sheep
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [C] | [Gm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [C] | [Dm] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
I am the gate. Whoev[C]er enters through [Gm]me will be [Dm]saved
I came that they may have [C]life, and have [Gm]it in abundance
[Dm]I have other [C]sheep that are not [Gm]of this fold
[Bb]There will be one [C]flock, one [Dm]shepherd
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]They know his voice
One [C]flock, one [Dm]shepherd
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
